Decision: AVOID, conviction 3. The fall came from the business itself, not market panic, so it is not a buying opportunity yet.

**Why it fell:** Reddit's third-quarter 10-Q, filed 2026-10-30, said search traffic was down. It also warned that user growth could weaken further in the fourth quarter. Google's AI summaries are the named cause. US daily users fell 5% from the previous quarter, and the stock dropped about 30% in a day to 91.73.

**Why not buy:** The financials are still excellent and the stock is cheaper than its peers on earnings and cash flow. But the company's new risk factors say AI tools can replace visits to the site and content licences may not be renewed. Until another quarter shows the US audience holding steady, the growth that would justify buying is unproven.

**Things to know:**
- **No entry price this time:** I set it to null. A lower price wouldn't change the decision; a 10-Q showing US daily users stabilising would.
- **Fair value set aside:** the fact sheet's mechanical fair value of 316.29 rests on revenue multiples from Reddit's loss-making early years as a public company. I added overrides that use the peer median of 4.5x instead, so Python will recalculate it much lower.
- **My 12-month scenarios:** bull 120 (25%), base 95 (45%), bear 62 (30%).
- **Watch triggers:** if the operating margin falls below 20% or the cash-flow margin below 25%, the weekly scan will catch it automatically.

